                "text": "If Congress doesn\u2019t act, nearly 22 million Americans will see their health insurance premiums more than DOUBLE on average. Senate Republicans are standing in the way, even though thousands of their constituents will see costs go way up.\n\nIn Alabama, 447,000 Americans.\nIn Alaska, 24,000 Americans.\nIn Arkansas, 144,000 Americans.\nIn Florida, 4,473,000 Americans.\nIn Idaho, 101,000 Americans.\nIn Indiana, 290,000 Americans.\nIn Iowa, 118,000 Americans.\nIn Kansas, 182,000 Americans.\nIn Kentucky, 77,000 Americans.\nIn Louisiana, 276,000 Americans.\nIn Maine, 54,000 Americans.\nIn Mississippi, 320,000 Americans.\nIn Missouri, 383,000 Americans.\nIn Montana, 67,000 Americans.\nIn North Carolina, 888,000 Americans.\nIn North Dakota, 38,000 Americans.\nIn Ohio, 514,000 Americans.\nIn Oklahoma, 290,000 Americans.\nIn Pennsylvania, 422,000 Americans.\nIn South Carolina, 588,000 Americans.\nIn South Dakota, 30,000 Americans.\nIn Tennessee, 593,000 Americans.\nIn Texas, 3,714,000 Americans.\nIn Utah, 395,000 Americans.\nIn West Virginia, 227,000 Americans.\nIn Wisconsin, 272,000 Americans.\nIn Wyoming, 43,000 Americans.\n\nWe\u2019re barreling toward a tipping point for American families.",
